amend='''\n\n# 13. v2.7.0 PROJECTCHAT TAB INTERACTION AMENDMENT — 2026-08-11\n\nThe BotsChat working name is retired. The client type is now visibly named **ProjectChat**. The internal persisted value `clientType: "botschat"` remains temporarily for backward compatibility with existing local/SOT state.\n\n- Right-clicking a live ProjectChat session tab opens a context menu with **Rename ›**, **Assign ›**, and **Customize ›**.\n- Rename opens a leaf editor; Enter calls the governed `sessions.patch` label update and returns focus to the project that was open when the menu was invoked.\n- Assign opens a Project omnisearch. Plain partial terms match anywhere, `*` is a wildcard, and `-term` excludes matches.\n- Tapping a Project result moves the session to that Project and returns focus to the existing/origin Project; assignment does not navigate the operator away.\n- Pressing Enter on an exact Project name assigns to it. Pressing Enter on a non-existent name creates that Project, moves the session, and still returns focus to the origin Project.\n- Customize persists per-session tab background color, font color, and font size in Project state and therefore in the GitHub SOT. Reset removes the customization.\n- Dragging tabs within a normal Project reorders the Project's persistent session sequence.\n- Dragging a tab onto a different Project continues to move the session, not copy it, and preserves the current Project focus.\n- The tab × remains governed soft delete to Recycle Bin.\n\n## Graveyard additions\n\n**G-031 — BotsChat visible product name.** Retired; the client is ProjectChat.\n\n**G-032 — Context assignment that navigates away from the operator's current Project.** Buried. Assignment is an organizational action; the current workspace remains the focus anchor.\n\n**G-033 — Non-persistent visual tab tweaks.** Buried. Per-tab customization is persistent Project/SOT state.\n'''
if '# 13. v2.7.0 PROJECTCHAT TAB INTERACTION AMENDMENT' not in g:g+=amend
GOV.write_text(g,encoding='utf-8')

